/ Task 30f: staged rollout control. Only rendered for someone who can
/ already manage this release (upload/edit/delete) -- rollout is a
/ per-release decision at the same ownership level as play_store_target,
/ not an org-wide editorial toggle, so it lives here rather than under a
/ separate Admin:: namespace.
/ Task 27f-b2: the form PATCHes the nested resource route (`channel_release_path`); the friendly
/ `/:channel/:id` route is GET-only, so a PATCH there fell into the not-found catch-all.
- if policy(release).update?
  .card
    .card-header
      h3.card-title = t('releases.show.rollout')
    .card-body.space-y-2
      div class="flex items-center gap-2"
        - badge_class = { 'active' => 'info', 'halted' => 'warning', 'complete' => 'success' }[release.rollout_status] || 'secondary'
        span.badge class="text-bg-#{badge_class}" = t("releases.show.rollout_status_badges.#{release.rollout_status}")
        span.opacity-60 = t('releases.show.rollout_percentage', percentage: release.rollout_percentage)

      = simple_form_for release, url: channel_release_path(release.channel, release), method: :patch, html: { class: 'flex flex-wrap items-end gap-2' } do |f|
        = f.input :rollout_percentage, as: :integer, input_html: { min: 0, max: 100, style: 'width: 6rem' }, label: t('releases.show.rollout_percentage_label'), wrapper_html: { class: 'mb-0' }
        = f.input :rollout_status, collection: Release.rollout_statuses.keys, include_blank: false, label: t('releases.show.rollout_status_label'), wrapper_html: { class: 'mb-0' }
        = f.button :submit, t('releases.show.rollout_update'), class: 'd-btn d-btn-sm'
